        "title": "Image Formation - The Camera Model",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Read left to right: a rigid transform `[R|t]` moves the point into the camera's frame;\nperspective division collapses depth; the intrinsic matrix `K` converts to pixel units;\nsampling and a color filter turn continuous irradiance into a discrete RGB array."
    },
